      "content": "The idea that you're a burden is a harsh narrative your mind is telling you, but it's not the truth of your existence. When your entire purpose dissolves, it feels like a dead end because you've been operating on a very rigid foundation. Instead of trying to \"reconnect\" to a lost self, perhaps you can start by acknowledging the quiet, small parts of you that are still there—the simple things you still feel or notice.",
